[[2047,15,8,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay J60 controls\nthe circuit for the rear electric windows (as well as the sun roof\nand heated seats: see \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234128\">E3060</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              e \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234156\">E3075</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ). .</p><p>The coil of the relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is energized\nwhen the ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99, while the supply at the relay contact arrives from the battery, through\nthe line for maxifuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J/B2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99).</p><p>This supply passes through the rear electric\nwindow fuses \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B18</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F3</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99, which guarantee the protection of the circuit,\nand arrives at the switches on the driver&#x27;s door (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H45</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               left\nand \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               right). The supply of the switches is therefore controlled\nby the ignition (INT/A) and they are connected to earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (in\nthis way they are also lit up when the ignition is switched on).</p><p>When these switches are operated, they send\ncommand signals (positive and negative) to the switches in the rear\ndoors and from there to the (left) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and right \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N66</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               motors:\nreversing the signals according to the contact which is closed determines\nthe direction of rotation of the actual motor.</p><p>The same supply controlled by the ignition\n(INT/A) also reaches the switches in the rear doors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H53</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\npassing through the safety switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H55</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , but only if it is\nin the go ahead position. If this is not the case, the supply to\nthe rear door switches is  stopped.</p><p>As with the front switches, when the rear\nswitches are activated, they send command signals (positive and\nnegative) to the (left) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and (right) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N66</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               motors:\nreversing the signals according to the contact which has been closed, determines\nthe direction of rotation of the actual motor.</p>"]]